  "lineage": "Sung repertoire of the Tausug of Jolo and the Sulu Archipelago in which the gabbang bamboo xylophone, often joined by the biola (violin), accompanies songs such as the sindil, a bantering sung exchange between a man and a woman. The religious and moral chants lugu and tarasul are sung unaccompanied. The fiddle card stands in for the biola.",
